# No "table", "circuit", "aisle", or "walk" rhetoric

Do not use the words **table** / **tables**, **circuit** / **circuits**, **aisle** / **aisles**, or **walk** / **walks** / **walking** in user-facing copy, headings, kickers, buttons, badges, empty states, or mockup descriptions anywhere on the site.

Use plain, direct language instead:

| Avoid | Use instead |
| --- | --- |
| On their table / On the tables / Stall table / Table items | Menu, Products, What they sell, Items, Menu items |
| Market hall circuit / On their circuit / Neighbourhood circuit | Markets, Where they sell, Market locations, Neighbourhoods |
| Aisle / Product aisle / Market aisle / Peer aisle stalls | Category, Product category, Specialty, Similar vendors / Other stalls |
| Market walk / Neighbourhood walk / Neighbourhood market walks / Worth the walk | Neighbourhood, Neighbourhood markets, Where they sell |

```tsx
// BAD
<p className="type-kicker">Published stall table</p>
<h2>Market hall circuit</h2>
<span>Compare in pies and sweets aisle</span>
<h2>Neighbourhood market walks</h2>

// GOOD
<p className="type-kicker">Menu &amp; products</p>
<h2>Markets &amp; hours</h2>
<span>Compare in pies and sweets</span>
<h2>Neighbourhood markets</h2>
```

A place note can still say a market sits along walkways. Code names such as `home-walkthrough` are not copy. The welcome panel is a welcome note in user-facing text.
